# Tooltip Styling

## Summary

This document provides the standard tooltip pattern to match navigation menu styling. It covers:

- **Standard Pattern**: Complete tooltip implementation with RTL support
- **RTL Support**: Direction-aware text in tooltip content
- **Styling**: Global theme styles, delays, and arrow configuration
- **Cursor on Hover**: Use a distinct cursor when hovering the tooltip trigger (e.g. `cursor: "help"` for info icons)
- **Key Points**: Always include arrow, proper delays, `placement="bottom"`, and cursor where appropriate

Tooltips should match the navigation menu styling and include full RTL support for Hebrew language.

## 🎨 Tooltip Styling

### Standard Tooltip Pattern

**ALWAYS use this pattern to match navigation menu styling:**

```typescript
import { Tooltip } from "@mui/material";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { i18n } = useTranslation();
const isHebrewUser = i18n.language === "he";

<Tooltip
    title={t("tooltip.text")}
    arrow
    enterDelay={300}
    leaveDelay={100}
    placement="bottom"
    PopperProps={{
        sx: {
            "& .MuiTooltip-tooltip": {
                direction: isHebrewUser ? "rtl" : "ltr",
            },
        },
    }}
>
    {/* Your component - add cursor for icon/trigger */}
    <IconComponent sx={{ cursor: "help" }} />
</Tooltip>
```

For report builder and shared report UI, prefer `getRTLTooltipProps(i18n)` from `@/utils/reportFieldUtils` — it applies the same defaults (`placement="bottom"`, delays, arrow, RTL text direction).

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Global theme styles defined in `app/theme.ts` (don't override)
- ✅ Always include `arrow` prop
- ✅ Use `enterDelay={300}` and `leaveDelay={100}`
- ✅ **Always use `placement="bottom"`** — do not default to `top`, `left`, or `right`
- ✅ RTL support via `PopperProps` with `direction` on tooltip content
- ✅ **Cursor on hover**: Set `cursor: "help"` on the tooltip trigger (e.g. info icon) so users see a help cursor when hovering; use `cursor: "pointer"` for clickable triggers

**Reference:** See `app/[locale]/app/AppShell.tsx` for navigation menu tooltip implementation.

### Cursor on Hover

When the tooltip wraps an icon or other trigger that only shows information (no click action), set a distinct cursor so users know they can hover for details:

- **Info / help tooltips**: Use `cursor: "help"` on the trigger (e.g. `<InfoIcon sx={{ cursor: "help" }} />`).
- **Clickable triggers**: Use `cursor: "pointer"` if the element also has an onClick.
- **Navigation / buttons**: Rely on default cursor or `pointer` as appropriate; no need to add `help` unless the primary affordance is “hover for tooltip”.
